<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 467)</h2>
<p><b>Optimised media — heavy sequences play light, originals stay the truth.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>File ▸ Optimise This Shot / Whole Session for Playback</b> renders a light local stand-in for image sequences: HEVC 10-bit, half res above HD, keeping your aspect. It asks once where to keep them — somewhere easy to find and safe to delete.</li>
<li><b>Your grade still works on them.</b> The stand-in bakes only the input transform, into a log curve, so it matches the original through any grade, look or display. Nothing is baked in that you'd want to change later.</li>
<li><b>Frame numbers are the original's.</b> A render numbered 993–1042 reads 993–1042 on the stand-in, never 1–50.</li>
<li><b>Grabs, exports and reports always use the original</b> — media and colour both. Verified pixel-identical to working without a stand-in.</li>
<li>A cyan OPTIMISED badge shows while you're on a stand-in. A re-rendered shot is detected and ignored rather than showing you yesterday's picture.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
